  "explains": "invoice_list in billing/views.py changes (its body: the line that builds the answer). It is a plain function view, and nothing restricts its methods, so the route answers every method: ANY. The URLconf says where it is mounted: config/urls.py includes billing.urls under billing/ (a string module path), and billing/urls.py has path(\"invoices/\", views.invoice_list). The full path is billing/ + invoices/, normalised without the trailing slash: ANY /billing/invoices, with the evidence of the path() line and then the include line. config/urls.py also imports billing.views, as billing_views, but only to name legacy_year, so it is excluded by narrowing; billing/urls.py names invoice_list and is the caller. The test file imports billing.views and is a unit test. On the web side INVOICES_URL is \"/billing/invoices/\" (the trailing slash is dropped), apiGet is a GET, and it fits only the list route; fetchInvoices is called by InvoiceListPage, mounted at /billing/invoices. The other pages call other routes (the detail route has a parameter segment the client literal list URL cannot fit, and the monthly report has its own route) and are not reached.",
